From 4b7f74bd94389d940491b3989e71f122783440c4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude (Cowork)" <botirbekshermatov563@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 10:39:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Rebuild storefront: SVG body guide, original package art,
 working admin panel

The published page never rendered its 3D block (model-viewer loaded a
relative .glb that does not exist there) and every product photo was a
blocked external Unsplash URL, so cards showed broken images. Checkout
relied on prompt()/alert(), which sandboxed frames ignore.

- Replace the 3D model with an original interactive inline-SVG body
  guide: eight hotspots, keyboard accessible, filters the catalogue.
- Replace all external photos with original SVG package illustrations
  (box, blister, syrup, dropper, effervescent, gel, sachet); type and
  hue are editable per product.
- Real checkout form with validation, promo codes, delivery threshold,
  toast notifications and an order record; Telegram hand-off kept.
- Working admin panel at #admin: KPI overview with status/revenue
  charts, product CRUD with live card preview, categories, orders with
  status changes, site settings, JSON export/import, factory reset.
- Persistence layer: shared artifact database when available, browser
  localStorage otherwise, with the same API for both.
- Storefront additions: wishlist, compare up to three products, price /
  stock / discount filters, grid-list toggle, FAQ, customer order
  history, mobile menu, correct Russian plurals.
- index.html and preview.html are now the same single-file build.

Verified in Chromium: 15 interaction flows pass with no console errors.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GFX4UK3tbHgJjBERzzT7fA
